 "**Past perfect tense** (had + past participle) shows the earlier of two past actions; the later action takes the simple past. *When the delegates arrived, the speaker had already begun.*",
 "**Prefixes giving opposite meanings:** un-, im-, dis-, in-, mis-, ir-, extra-. Examples: unpopular, disbelief, unimportant, disrespect, incorrect, discontinue, misunderstand, extraordinary, uninteresting, impossible.",
 "**Binomials** (fixed pairs): sink or swim, on and off, mix and match, all or nothing, part and parcel, pick and choose, sooner or later, leaps and bounds.",
 "**Idioms of learning:** hit the books (study seriously), draw a blank (be unable to remember), learn the ropes (understand how to do something), rack one's brain (think very hard), learn by heart (memorise), burn the midnight oil (study late into the night).",
